  "reasoning": "The patient presents with stomach pain that worsens when lying down or hunching over, pain triggered by hot or acidic foods, and occasional loose stools. These symptoms align precisely with Reference [1], which describes a burning feeling in the stomach worse when lying down, pain after eating spicy or acidic foods, and loose stools, mapping to peptic ulcer disease. While gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) can also involve discomfort when lying down and after eating acidic foods, the training references associate GERD primarily with heartburn, indigestion, and chest pain, without mentioning loose stools. The specific combination of stomach pain and loose stools factually rules out GERD and establishes peptic ulcer disease as the correct single-unit diagnosis.",
